       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- **Per dose:** The usual maximum single dose is 800 mg. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Per day:** The labeled maximum for prescription use is 3,200 mg/day. This order would give 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** Acute kidney injury, GI bleeding or perforation, and cardiovascular events. Higher doses don't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove these risks.\n\nWas this a typo or a unit mix-up? Some possibilities:\n\n- **400 mg QID** (1,600 mg/day) is a common analgesic regimen.\n- **800 mg TID** (2,400 mg/day) is a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, which could be given as 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg QID as written, tell me that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale to put in the order note. I'd still recommend a pharmacy review first."
      }
     ],
